  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under refill protocol RBC-RX-05: 7 items closed, 0 left open. Two lisinopril refills were not done: results that arrived while I worked raised a safety flag, so I cancelled the renewals I had already sent and sent the patients corrections. Both need your review.\n\n**Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg – not refilled; needs your review**\n- At first I renewed it for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0001). His August potassium of 5.9 didn't count because the sample was hemolyzed. The last valid potassium was 4.5 in January. I also ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0002).\n- While I worked, a new St. Brigid BMP arrived (drawn 10/20, good sample): potassium 5.8. That is at or above the protocol's 5.5 cut-off, so I cancelled the renewal.\n- I created an urgent review task for you (task-t0013) and sent him a corrected message (comm-t0015).\n- His hernia repair is now scheduled for 11/12.\n- The repeat BMP order (sr-t0002) is still open.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030), lisinopril 20 mg – not refilled; needs your review**\n- At first I renewed it for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0003).\n- The lab then corrected his 10/06 creatinine from 1.36 to 1.49. That is 35.5% above his 1.10 from before the 9/18 dose increase. A rise over 30% within 4 weeks of a dose increase counts the same as a high potassium, so I cancelled the renewal.\n- I created an urgent review task for you (task-t0014) and sent him a corrected message (comm-t0016).\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030), metformin 1000 mg twice daily – renewed**\n- 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004). His corrected kidney function (eGFR) is 58, still at or above the 45 cut-off, and his outside HbA1c from 8/19 was 7.1%.\n- This one order answers his message and both pharmacy requests (one of which arrived while I worked).\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031)**\n- Lisinopril 10 mg: 30-day supply with no refills (mr-t0005), and I ordered a BMP (sr-t0006). His last BMP was drawn 10/20/2025, just outside 12 months. He had a visit on 9/28/26. A potassium of 4.6 measured on its own arrived while I worked, but on its own it doesn't count as a BMP, so this decision stands.\n- Metformin 500 mg twice daily: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). His eGFR is 92 and his 9/28 HbA1c was 6.9%. I didn't use the 10/14 eGFR of 39 because it was marked entered in error.\n\n**Things to know**\n- **No active lisinopril order for Odum or Price:** placing each renewal automatically stopped their original orders (mr-00283, mr-00295). Cancelling the renewals didn't restart them. Your review tasks point to those original orders.\n- **Notes and replies:** I wrote a chart note for each patient (doc-t0017, doc-t0018, doc-t0019) and sent each patient a reply.\n- **Results queue:** I read the three results that arrived for these patients (inbox-a0001, a0002, a0004) but left them open because that queue wasn't part of this request. I didn't touch any other results queue items, including the open critical potassium results for other patients.",
